{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SCOPE EXTENDED — the same defect is live on the DIRECT-ANTHROPIC path, confirmed by a production\nobservation, not only on Bedrock.\n\nOPERATOR REPORT: the code-review bot logs \"Sampling parameters ['temperature'] are not supported by\n'claude-opus-4-8'\" on essentially every call.\n\nVERIFIED, three ways:\n1. `capabilities_for(\"anthropic:claude-opus-4-8\").supports_temperature` was TRUE — the override table\n   covered only the Bedrock-prefixed ids, so rebar kept SENDING temperature on the Anthropic path.\n2. That log line is emitted verbatim by pydantic-ai at models/anthropic.py:641, from\n   `_drop_unsupported_sampling_settings`.\n3. `models/bedrock.py` contains ZERO occurrences of that helper. So it is ONE defect with TWO symptoms:\n   the Anthropic adapter silently DROPS the parameter and warns; the Bedrock adapter has no such drop\n   and the call 400s. The earlier Bedrock-only framing of this ticket was too narrow.\n\nWHY THIS IS MORE THAN LOG NOISE. The warning is the visible half. The real cost is that a pass pinning\ntemperature=0 for determinism silently does not get it. `workflow/gates/code-review.yaml:155` pins\n`temperature: 0` on the Pass-2 verify step, with the stated reason: \"Greedy Pass-2 verification:\nre-running the same finding must not resample its narrow yes/no verification and drift impact/validity.\"\nAnd code review has NO verifier downgrade — it never calls `resolve_verifier_model`, so ALL of its\npasses (base/round_a/round_b, verify, coach) run on cfg.model = claude-opus-4-8. So code-review's Pass-2\nhas been resampling in production, which is a plausible source of review nondeterminism. That is a\ncorrectness finding, not a cosmetic one.\n\nFIX: added the BARE ids `claude-opus-4-8` and `claude-opus-4-7` to the override table. The table keys on\nthe bare id (`_model_id_of` strips the provider prefix), so these cover BOTH `anthropic:<id>` and the\nbare string, while the `us.`/`global.` entries continue to cover Bedrock. Withdrawing the parameter is\nWIRE-IDENTICAL to having it dropped downstream — the same request goes out either way — but it removes\nthe per-call warning and, more importantly, removes the false belief that greedy decoding is in effect.\n\nONE PRE-EXISTING TEST WAS CORRECTED, not weakened. `test_supports_temperature_defaults_true_for_\neverything_else` used `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8` as its example of an UNLISTED model, asserting it kept\ntemperature. That exemplar encoded a fact this observation disproves. The test's intent (\"the denylist\nmust not leak\") and its assertion count are unchanged; the example moved to models that are genuinely\nunlisted and measured to accept temperature (`anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6`, `openai:gpt-4o`).\n\nFOLLOW-ON worth its own consideration, NOT done here: rebar sends temperature whenever configured, and\nlearns it was ignored only from a provider log line. A pass that REQUIRES greedy decoding cannot tell\nwhether it got it. Consider making `supports_temperature=False` visible where determinism is assumed —\ne.g. Pass-2 warning once when it pins temperature=0 on a model whose capability record says the\nparameter is withdrawn. That is exactly the \"green signal whose measurement could not be verified\" shape\nepic 3147 exists for."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785462877158187001,"uuid":"3aeb3faa-0078-4bdb-bd14-fe7d9393bc55"}